  "worked_solution": "The difference of squares formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{2}-{b}^{2}=(a+b)(a-b)\n$$\n\nNotice that the expression in parenthesis can be written as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{16}{y}^{4}-{z}^{4}{w}^{8}=({({x}^{8}{y}^{2})}^{2}-{({z}^{2}{w}^{4})}^{2})\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n({({x}^{8}{y}^{2})}^{2}-{({z}^{2}{w}^{4})}^{2})=({x}^{8}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}{w}^{4})({x}^{8}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}{w}^{4})\n$$\n\nFinally, we notice that the expression in the second set of parentheses is also a difference of squares. Therefore, the expression can be factored further, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{8}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}{w}^{4})({x}^{8}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}{w}^{4}) & =({x}^{8}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}{w}^{4})({({x}^{4}y)}^{2}-{(z{w}^{2})}^{2}) \\\\  & =({x}^{8}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}{w}^{4})({x}^{4}y+z{w}^{2})({x}^{4}y-z{w}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
